From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:45:16 +0000
Subject: stick-deadzones: a radial deadzone for each stick of a physical
 controller (DM_STICK_DEADZONE_L / _R)

A worn or drifting stick reaches the game as the controller reports it. DM_STICK_DEADZONE_L and DM_STICK_DEADZONE_R take a whole percent of the travel (1..50): inside it the stick reads centred, outside it the rest of the travel is rescaled so a full push still reads full. Unset or 0 leaves the stick as reported. The deadzone sits in dm_pad_set_player, which every physical controller passes through; keyboard, touch and scripted input do not use it. NXForge's sidebar sets both (Controller page).

Origin: v0lumehi's commit 41d7c5eb in widmonstertony/nxnative (MIT), forwarded upstream as seedds/nxnative#2101; drop this patch when upstream has it.
